{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Two live pure birds.</b> All pure birds are called צפור, as it is said (Deuteronomy 14:11) ״כל צפור טהורה תאכלו״ — this excludes impure birds and excludes forbidden birds, such as the bird of the seduced city (צפור עיר הנדחת) or a bird that killed a life; and therefore it needed to specify טהורות, that it be a pure and permitted bird." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״שתי צפרים חיות טהורות״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: let his offering be צפרים, whose sound chirps (מצפצף); let the sound come and atone for the sound." "<b>And cedar wood and scarlet yarn and hyssop.</b> Scripture took hold of the greatest and the smallest of all species of plants, and so Scripture too mentions concerning Solomon (1 Kings 5:13) ״from the cedar that is in Lebanon even unto the hyssop that springs out of the wall,״ and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: what is the remedy for this one who grows proud and lofty like a cedar? He should humble himself like hyssop, and it will be atoned for him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:21.132262996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}